From: AIwork4me <AIwork4me@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:40:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] MIOpen: make remaining RTC kernel std includes
 self-contained

Complete kernel-source self-containment for the two remaining unguarded
host-library includes found by auditing all runtime-compiled kernel
closures.

radix.hpp included <limits> unconditionally. Its
std::numeric_limits<int32_t/int64_t>::max() uses are parse-time-checked
template-definition names, so they are replaced by the equivalent
__INT32_MAX__/__INT64_MAX__ predefined macros in every compilation
path: the substitution is unconditional, not runtime-compile-only;
only the include selection is path-dependent (the runtime-compile arm
needs just the fixed-width typedefs from miopen_cstdint.hpp, while the
offline arm still includes <limits> for transitive users).

tensor_view.hpp included <initializer_list> unconditionally; it now
selects the real header through an availability probe when a standard
library is reachable and falls back to a clang-lowered freestanding
definition otherwise. Unlike the type_traits/utility probes of the
first commit, this probe is deliberately not HIP-version-gated and
carries no partial-STL cross-probe: both headers it selects between
define the same single class, so a mixed environment cannot produce
conflicting definitions.
